Terraform Tip of the Day: Why You Should Always Use Remote State

If you're still storing your Terraform state locally…you're one accidental rm -rf away from losing track of your entire infrastructure.
And trust me you don’t want to learn this lesson the hard way.

Here’s why remote state is now a must-have, not an option 

✅ 1. Collaboration Becomes Easy
Multiple engineers can apply changes without state conflicts.
 No more:
“State is locked, who’s running terraform apply?”

✅ 2. Automatic State Locking
Remote backends (S3 + DynamoDB, GCS, Azure Blob, Terraform Cloud) prevent two people from updating the state at the same time.
This stops:
Corruption
Overwrites
Race conditions

✅ 3. Versioning Saves You From Disaster
Pushed a wrong change?
Remote backends with versioning let you roll back your state instantly.
Better than trying to recover a deleted local file.

✅ 4. Security You Can Trust
Encrypted at rest.
Encrypted in transit.
And not sitting on someone’s laptop.
Your infrastructure deserves better.

💡 Pro Tip
For AWS:
Use S3 (state) + DynamoDB (locking) → It’s the industry standard combo.
